+COMMAND:
+PYTHONPATH=/reference python3 <script invoking
+tools.klean_preflight.check_generation with full subcommand recording>
+
+RESULT:
+COMMAND: PYTHONPATH=/reference tools.klean_preflight.check_generation(/reference/k-proof, /reference/lemma-discovery.json, /reference/klean-generation, toolchain_lock=/reference/klean-toolchain.lock.json)
+SUBCOMMAND: ["lake", "clean"]
+CWD: /tmp/klean-preflight-f5qpavzp/project
+TIMEOUT: 600
+EXIT_CODE: 1
+OUTPUT_BEGIN
+error: could not detect the configuration of the Lake installation
+OUTPUT_END
+OUTPUT_SHA256: dfce1e7d6849bcb01696e698fae3345a66f15495d7e36f99ac1293476a5bd045
+TRACEBACK_FINAL:
+tools.klean_preflight.KleanPreflightError: lake clean failed (1): error: could not detect the configuration of the Lake installation
+
+DIAGNOSIS COMMANDS AND RESULTS:
+command -v lake
+/opt/elan/bin/lake
+
+lake --version
+Lake version 5.0.0-src+ba2cbbf (Lean version 4.22.0)
+
+lean --version
+error: failed to locate application
+
+python3 -c "import os; print(os.getpid()); print(os.readlink(f'/proc/{os.getpid()}/exe'))"
+PID returned inside namespace: 3
+FileNotFoundError: /proc/3/exe
+
+readlink /proc/self/exe
+/usr/bin/readlink
+
+The Lean 4.22 runtime implementation of lean_io_app_path reads
+/proc/<getpid()>/exe. This sandbox exposes /proc/self/exe but does not expose
+the namespace PID as /proc/<pid>, causing IO.appPath and Lake installation
+detection to fail.
+
+WORKAROUND:
+Compiled /tmp/audit-work/lean_proc_exe_shim.c into
+/tmp/audit-work/lean_proc_exe_shim.so. The shim changes only readlink requests
+matching /proc/<pid>/exe to /proc/self/exe. It does not alter any mounted audit
+input, generated source, checker, or toolchain file.
+
+VALIDATION:
+LD_PRELOAD=/tmp/audit-work/lean_proc_exe_shim.so lean --version
+Lean (version 4.22.0, x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu, commit ba2cbbf09d4978f416e0ebd1fceeebc2c4138c05, Release)
